way the new "Spaces Shoes" are. The heel was lower than the
toe...supposed to do something "natural" to one's feet. I didn't like
'em, and they were unsightly, too.

Shoes are shoes. I mostly wear Teva sport sandals, even in the winter.
Heat loss through the feet is minimal, and it is usually through the
soles. The Tevas have thick insulating soles, so no problem.

