When Earth Shoes first came out they started a fad for boxy-toe (i.e., foot
shaped) shoes that lasted a few years, but that fad has long faded.  Alas for
me, since I have wide toes and that was the only period in my life when I was
ever able to procure comfortable shoes without a prolonged search (and it's
been getting harder every year).

I never bought Earth Shoes, but I remembered them when foot shaped shoes
started becoming rare, and a couple of years ago I finally asked a salesman at
a shoe store what had become of them.  He told me that it turned out that Earth
Shoes' patented "inverted heel" caused permanent knee damage in people who did
large amounts of walking when wearing them (e.g., folks like mail carriers) and
that, as a result, the company was obliterated by product liability lawsuits.

I was delighted for once to hear that nonsensical ecobabble (if you will recall
their ads) had come back to bite its emitter in the face, but I don't really
know if this story is true or not.

